{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"live","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"endpoint","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fetchTimeout","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","text":"TimeInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 10, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cacheLifetime","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","text":"TimeInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 3600, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"session","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSURLSession","text":"URLSession","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = .shared) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SwiduxKillswitch0B7ServiceV","text":"KillswitchService","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxKillswitch\/documentation\/SwiduxKillswitch\/KillswitchService"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The endpoint must be HTTPS (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"text":" is allowed only for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost"},{"text":" \/","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"127.0.0.1"},{"text":" development servers) — the killswitch is a remote control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"channel and must not be tamperable in transit, regardless of the host","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app’s ATS configuration. The transfer is aborted the moment the response","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"body exceeds 1 MB (it is streamed, never fully buffered past the cap),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and non-2xx statuses are treated as fetch failures (the plugin then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"falls back to its cache).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchTimeout"},{"text":" bounds the whole fetch, headers and body together — not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"just the gap between packets. A response trickled in a byte at a time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"still fails at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchTimeout"},{"text":", so the plugin reaches its cached verdict","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on schedule instead of waiting on a transfer that never ends. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchTimeout"},{"text":" that isn’t finite and positive (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"text":", say) sets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no deadline, leaving only the session’s own timeouts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-cache-is-the-other-input-path","text":"The cache is the other input path","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A cached config produces a verdict with exactly the authority a fetched","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one has, and it is reached without any successful fetch ever having","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"happened — launch offline and the failure path loads it directly. So it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is scoped and checked rather than trusted:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It lives in a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"bundle-scoped subdirectory","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" of the caches directory."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"On a non-sandboxed macOS build "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cachesDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/Library\/Caches"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shared by the whole user account, so a bare filename would have every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swidux app reading every other’s blocked verdict."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It records the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"endpoint it came from","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxKillswitch\/documentation\/SwiduxKillswitch\/KillswitchService\/loadCached","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" treats a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"payload written for a different one as absent. Repointing the endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore invalidates the cache rather than inheriting it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Neither of those makes the file authenticated. A process running as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user can still write it on a platform where the caches directory isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sandboxed — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxkillswitch\/killswitchservice\/live(endpoint:fetchtimeout:cachelifetime:session:)"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Production factory that fetches from a URL endpoint and caches to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the system Caches directory.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxKillswitch\/documentation\/SwiduxKillswitch\/KillswitchService\/live(endpoint:fetchTimeout:cacheLifetime:session:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"live","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"endpoint","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fetchTimeout","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cacheLifetime","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"session","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URLSession","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSURLSession"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SwiduxKillswitch0B7ServiceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"KillswitchService"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxKillswitch"}],"title":"live(endpoint:fetchTimeout:cacheLifetime:session:)","externalID":"s:16SwiduxKillswitch0B7ServiceV4live8endpoint12fetchTimeout13cacheLifetime7sessionAC10Foundation3URLV_S2dSo12NSURLSessionCtFZ","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Type Method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxKillswitch\/documentation\/SwiduxKillswitch","doc:\/\/SwiduxKillswitch\/documentation\/SwiduxKillswitch\/KillswitchService"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxKillswitch/documentation/SwiduxKillswitch/KillswitchService/loadCached":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"id